# P01.2 R8 live proof — codex-cli, session-engine.mjs (no CLI door, no dispatch.mjs)

Driver script (not committed elsewhere; copied here verbatim as evidence):
`p012-live-proof-driver-script.mjs`. It imports and calls ONLY
`openStandaloneSession`, `dispatchPrimaryTask`, `proposeConsult`,
`resumeSession` from `src/runner/coordination/session-engine.mjs` -- no
`child_process`, no `dispatch.mjs` CLI door, no other spawn path. Every
executor dispatch below went through
`session-engine.mjs -> createSessionAssignment()/executeAssignment()`, the
ONLY execution entry point this cell's engine ever calls.

Repo root / cwd for every invocation: `/home/vantt/projects/forgentX` (the
real repo, not a temp fixture -- this proof's objective genuinely reads this
repo's real `package.json`).

## Attempt 1 — config-tier stop (honest, not a dispatch/engine defect)

```
node p012-live-proof.mjs coord_p012_live_76055_codex codex-cli full
```
Full transcript: `codex-cli-attempt1-config-tier-stop.stdout.log` /
`.stderr.log`.

`openStandaloneSession` succeeded (manifest/events written). `dispatchPrimaryTask`
threw before any executor spawned:
```
RunnerConfigError: no model configured for policy tier "standard" under provider "codex".
    at resolvePolicyTierModel ... at resolveAssignmentDispatchPolicy ...
    at compileDispatchPlan ... at executeAssignment ...
    at createAndExecuteSessionTask (session-engine.mjs:199)
    at dispatchPrimaryTask (session-engine.mjs:300)
```
Root cause (confirmed by reading `.fgos/config.json` and
`src/runner/dispatch/resolve.mjs` directly, not guessed): the already-landed
P00.4 fix (`assignment-policy.mjs` now passes `codex-cli`'s real resolved
command `codex` into `deriveProviderFamily`, confirmed via
`grep -n deriveProviderFamily src/runner/dispatch/{assignment-policy,resolve}.mjs`)
correctly derives `providerModel: "codex"` for `codex-cli` (previously it
silently fell back to `"claude"`, P00.3/P00.4's own documented bug). But
`.fgos/config.json`'s `modelPolicies` table has no `codex` entry (only
`openai-codex`, used by the sibling `codex-pi`/`pi-herdr` executors, which
DO declare `providerModel: "openai-codex"` -- `codex-cli` itself declares
neither `providerModel` nor `provider`). This is a real, pre-existing
config-registration gap (same class P00.3/P00.4 already flagged, now
actually surfaced because the P00.4 fix stopped masking it) -- out of this
cell's scope to fix (`.fgos/config.json`/`resolve.mjs`/`assignment-policy.mjs`
are outside P01.2's touchable surface). Worked around, not patched, using an
existing caller-facing override already wired through this cell's own
`opts.cliOverride` passthrough: `cliOverride.model` short-circuits
`resolvePolicyTierModel` entirely (`assignment-policy.mjs`: `if
(cliOverride.model) { resolvedModel = cliOverride.model; ... }`), and
`codex-cli`'s own invocation template (`["exec",
"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox", "{prompt}"]`) never
substitutes a `{model}` token anyway (P00.3's own prior finding), so any
non-empty model string is safe to pass.

## Attempt 2 — genuine live dispatch, honest `no-evidence` partial (not fabricated)

```
node p012-live-proof.mjs coord_p012_live_76055_codex codex-cli resume gpt-5.5
```
Full transcript: `codex-cli-attempt2-no-evidence-partial.stdout.log` /
`.stderr.log`.

The real `codex` binary was genuinely invoked this time and answered
correctly: `agentClaim: {"status":"done","summary":"Root package.json has
name \"forgent\" and version \"0.1.0\"."}` -- but the RunResult classified
as `status: "no-evidence", confidence: "no-evidence"`, not `"done"`.
Traced the cause directly in `src/runner/dispatch/assignment.mjs`'s
`renderAssignmentPrompt` (unmodified by this cell): for a read-only
Assignment the prompt tells the worker `- Optional human-readable report:
<path>/agent-report.md` -- "Optional", so codex, correctly following the
literal prompt, wrote only `agent-result.json`. `assignment-runner.mjs`'s
`classifyRunEvidence` (also unmodified) requires a companion worker-produced
report artifact -- not just the self-attested JSON claim -- before a
read-only Assignment can reach `confidence: "reported"` (anti-fabrication
design: "Self-attested evidenceRefs strings never substitute for it"). This
is a real, honestly-recorded partial result, not a bug in this cell's
session engine or a fabricated pass -- fixed at the caller level (this
cell's own driver script, the level this engine's contract-building
functions leave under caller control) by explicitly naming
`agent-report.md` in `expectedOutputs`, exactly the same signal
`buildDeclaredAssignment` already auto-adds for declared read-only roles
(ADR-006) but `buildInlineAssignment` deliberately leaves to the caller.

