## Attempt 4 — second invocation: resume/re-dispatch the SAME session, zero duplicate runs (R7 live proof)

```
node p012-live-proof.mjs coord_p012_live_76229_codex2 codex-cli resume gpt-5.5
```
Full transcript: `codex-cli-run2-resume.stdout.log` / `.stderr.log`.

`dispatchPrimaryTask` returned `resumed: true`, the SAME `assignmentId`
(`asgn_...op_002`), and a RunResult byte-identical (JSON round-trip) to
attempt 3's -- read back off disk (`readLinkedRunResultFromDisk`), never
re-executed. `proposeConsult` for the SAME `specialistActorId` ("specialist")
also returned `resumed: true` and the SAME consult `assignmentId`
(`asgn_...op_003`), not rejected as a disallowed "second round" (this exact
scenario surfaced and was fixed during this proof -- see Gaps/Fix Evidence
in P01.2.md: the engine's original one-round check did not yet distinguish
"the same specialist actor resuming" from "a genuinely new specialist",
this run is the corrected engine).

Confirmed directly on disk after this second invocation:
```
ls .fgos/assignments/asgn_p01_2_live_proof_coordinator_op_002/runs/   -> 01   (only)
ls .fgos/assignments/asgn_p01_2_live_proof_coordinator_op_003/runs/   -> 01   (only)
```
No `02` run directory was created for either Assignment. Exit code: 0.

## Summary

Both R8 and R7's live-proof requirement are met with codex-cli: primary AND
consult both completed genuinely (`status: "done"`, `confidence:
"reported"`, real correct answers, zero repository mutation), and a second
full invocation against the same session produced zero duplicate
Assignments and zero duplicate Runs. Attempts 1-2 above are kept as honest,
non-fabricated evidence of two real config/prompt-shaping issues encountered
and worked around within this cell's own scope (a caller-side `cliOverride.model`
passthrough and caller-side `expectedOutputs` naming `agent-report.md`) --
neither required touching any Do-Not-Touch file.
